<!-- FAQ — single, clean section -->
<section class="tw-section-ivory">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center mb-5 tw-fade">
      <span class="tw-section-label">Common Questions</span>
      <h2>Before you reach out, <em style="color:var(--tw-gold);">here are some answers</em></h2>
      <hr class="tw-divider">
      <p style="max-width:520px;margin:1.25rem auto 0;">Here are the questions Shimul hears most often from people considering reaching out for the first time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="row g-4 tw-fade">
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>How do I know if therapy is right for me?</h4>
          <p>If you are asking that question, it probably is. Therapy is not only for people in crisis. It is for anyone who wants to understand themselves better, work through something that feels stuck, or simply have a dedicated space to process life. You do not need to be at a breaking point to benefit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>Does insurance cover psychotherapy in Ontario?</h4>
          <p>Many extended health benefit plans and Employee Assistance Programs cover sessions with a Registered Psychotherapist. OHIP does not cover private psychotherapy. Check with your provider before your first session. Shimul provides properly formatted receipts for insurance submission after each session.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>What is the difference between a psychotherapist and a psychologist?</h4>
          <p>Both are regulated mental health professionals in Ontario. Psychologists typically have doctoral-level training and can provide assessments and diagnoses. Registered Psychotherapists specialize in therapeutic treatment and talk therapy. For most people seeking emotional support, a Registered Psychotherapist is an excellent and often more accessible choice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>How long does therapy typically take?</h4>
          <p>There is no single answer. Some people find that six to ten sessions gives them what they need. Others benefit from longer-term support. The timeline depends entirely on your goals and the pace that feels right for you. Shimul will revisit this with you regularly throughout your work together.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>Is everything I say completely confidential?</h4>
          <p>Yes. Shimul is bound by CRPO ethical guidelines and Ontario privacy law. The only exceptions involve imminent risk of harm to yourself or others, or a court order. These exceptions are explained clearly in your intake documents before your first session. Your privacy is foundational to this work.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-6">
        <div class="tw-approach-card tw-card-static h-100">
          <h4>What if I need to cancel or reschedule?</h4>
          <p>Shimul simply asks for a minimum of 24 hours notice for cancellations or rescheduling. Sessions cancelled with less than 24 hours notice may be subject to the full session fee. This policy exists to respect the time of both Shimul and other clients who may need that appointment slot.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
document.getElementById('contactForm').addEventListener('submit', async function(e) {
  e.preventDefault();
  const formData = { name: this.name.value, email: this.email.value, subject: this.subject.value, message: this.message.value };
  try {
    const res = await fetch('/send-message', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify(formData) });
    const msg = document.getElementById('responseMsg');
    if (res.ok) { msg.style.display = 'block'; this.reset(); }
  } catch(err) { console.error(err); }
});
</script>
